This is indeed interesting - naively, those Tenpatti rates look exactly 
like what you would expect from a triangle term, and the Alagapuram case 
looks like a triangle term that "saturates" at some point.  Both of 
these are compatible with the possibility that what is needed is a local 
triangle term (with the locality condition being something that maxes 
out fast enough that one never gets a density explosion).  Kinship 
embeddedness and/or geography would be my first guesses about what might 
restrict edge dependence here (i.e., it might just be shared partners 
that are spatially local, or those that are embedded within a particular 
kinship configuration).

That would be my first take, FWIW.....

-Carter



